From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 16:56:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: clear radar state when the channel context
 is removed

When the last link leaves a channel context, mac80211 frees the
context without a radar change, so the phy keeps radar detection
marked on. A later channel set without a context, for example the
return to the old operating channel at the end of a scan, then starts
the radar detector or a CAC on a channel that no AP uses.

Clear the radar state together with the channel context. The next
channel context sets it again from its own configuration.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 channel.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/channel.c
+++ b/channel.c
@@ -70,8 +70,10 @@ void mt76_remove_chanctx(struct ieee8021
 		mt76_abort_scan(dev);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mutex);
-	if (phy->chanctx == ctx)
+	if (phy->chanctx == ctx) {
 		phy->chanctx = NULL;
+		phy->radar_enabled = false;
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mutex);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_remove_chanctx);
